TEXT 272 96 Left 4 ;line1
TEXT 496 96 Left 4 ;line2
TEXT -160 -48 Left 6 ;Bus1
TEXT 632 16 Left 5 ;Three phase fault at time=2s
TEXT -120 152 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=1m abstol=1m
TEXT -120 176 Left 2 !.tran 0 4 0 0.1m
TEXT 496 112 Left 2 ;Capacitive currents of line element I(U4:CE1,CE2,CE3)
TEXT 560 56 Left 2 ;Current at fault position high because the line capacitances of line2 are shorted !!\nThe current off the voltagesource is much smaller
TEXT 264 184 Left 2 ;Switcher phase2,3 opens after about 100ms \nSwitcher phase 1 remains closed (fault)\nso the three phase short circuit leads\nto a one pole earth fault\nwith higher voltages of phase 2,3\nTransient voltages are even higher because of capacitive\ncurrent flow due to\ncharging of capacitances of phase 2,3 to 1.73*U\nand discharging of capacitance of phase1 to zero\nThese currents flow through the inductivities of the\ncircuit and makes high voltages
TEXT 520 192 Left 2 ;HINT: To met the ioff condition of the switcher\none has to set the ioff current high for a high current\nand low for a low current. You can also make the\nmaximum stepsize smaller to have a shure timepoint\nwith i under ioff\nTest it with a lower value of ioff until the \ncondition is perhaps never met\n(no timepoint is under ioff)
